I commented on and closed the two issues this session's commits fixed. I left the other ten alone, with no comment, because this session did no work on them.

• #1180 (inline table like `directories = { deny = [...] }`): fixed in a86656ca, and closed. yoyo now refuses these lines instead of reading them. The warning says the line is valid TOML that yoyo doesn't read and has no effect. For directories and permissions it also says the rule is NOT in force. It then prints the user's line rewritten into the [directories] form yoyo does read. I added 12 rows to the test corpus, and a test checks that each rewrite reads the same as tomllib reads the original line. The comment names what's still open: an array split over several lines gets only a generic example, and [mcp_servers] followed by fs = {...} is now #1182.
• #1166 (retired `github` provider): fixed in 60146c31, and closed. The missed spot was the "unknown provider" error, which still listed github as a choice. github now sits in a separate list of retired providers. I also stopped yoyo from sending GITHUB_TOKEN to a user-supplied --base-url, which would have sent a credential to the wrong server. The comment says why the one remaining github branch in agent_builder.rs stays. It also notes a small leftover: in the REPL, /provider github with a base URL set switches to a generic default model. /provider custom behaves the same way, so that leftover isn't specific to this issue.

Before writing, I checked both comments against the commit messages and a grep of the source.
